  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2024-2025 EU voluntary contribution to the UN Resident Coordinator System through the ad hoc UN Special Purpose Trust Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(252, 252, 253); color: rgb(48, 48, 48);&quot;&gt;In May 2018, the UN Development System (UNDS) undertook a reform including the design of a reinvigorated Resident Coordinator System (RCS, launched in January 2019), to get UN Agencies/Programmes/Funds work together more efficiently at country level. In addition, UN Resident Coordinators (RCs) coordinate UN support to countries in implementing the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(252, 252, 253); color: rgb(48, 48, 48);&quot;&gt;The EU contributed EUR 73.4 million over 2019-23 to the RCS (part of the EU funds were coming from DG NEAR and FPI) &#xbf; namely, to the System functioning (EUR 44.2 million) and the development of more than 60 Integrated National Financial Frameworks under RCs&apos; leadership. Another EUR 30 million have been mobilised by DG INTPA for 2023-26 to specifically boost, under RCs&#xbf; leadership, digital transformation in a set of Partner Countries.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(252, 252, 253); color: rgb(48, 48, 48);&quot;&gt;The present EU (DG INTPA) contribution is meant to continue support to the functioning of the UN RC System. The EU commitment is political, in favour of the pursuit of the UNDS reform, the empowerment of the RCS, and the strengthening of the global EU partnership with the UN at country level in line with EU priorities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(252, 252, 253); color: rgb(48, 48, 48);&quot;&gt;The EU financial support (8 million EUR in 2025 and 8 million EUR in 2026) shall be channelled through a pillar-assessed UNS entity, in indirect management.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
